From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:34:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: Add a quirk that keeps the host router's links
 out of CLx

Some hosts must not use CL states on the links of their own router. Add
an NHI quirk that gives the host router QUIRK_NO_CLX, which some host
routers already get from the router quirk table. The connection manager
only enables CL states on the first link, so in effect this keeps CL
states off in the whole domain.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit cacda34c694b884d2daa8c5147a244a2863a33bc)
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h | 2 ++
 drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c  | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
index 2707adf621..4e2e914668 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
@@ -214,6 +214,8 @@ struct tb_nhi_ops {
  * PCIe host kept its link up: the tunnels are still active on resume.
  */
 #define QUIRK_KEEP_TUNNELS				BIT(7)
+/* The links of the host router must not enter CL states. */
+#define QUIRK_NO_HOST_CLX				BIT(8)
 
 /* Host display policies are independent of which optional hooks are installed. */
 #define TB_HOST_DP_NOTIFY		BIT(0)
diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
index 5a8233150b..c646171303 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
@@ -3190,6 +3190,10 @@ static int tb_start(struct tb *tb, bool reset)
 	 * on these machines.
 	 */
 	tb->root_switch->no_usb3_bw_alloc = tb->nhi->quirks & QUIRK_NO_USB3_BW_ALLOC;
+	if (tb->nhi->quirks & QUIRK_NO_HOST_CLX) {
+		tb->root_switch->quirks |= QUIRK_NO_CLX;
+		tb_sw_dbg(tb->root_switch, "disabling CL states\n");
+	}
 
 	ret = tb_switch_configure(tb->root_switch);
 	if (ret) {
